# React components

## Stack

- React 19 + Next.js 16 App Router
- Tailwind CSS v4 — use utility classes; avoid inline styles unless dynamic (e.g. brand colors from data)
- Icons: `lucide-react`

## Structure

```tsx
"use client"; // only if needed

import { ... } from "@/components/shop";

type Props = { ... };

export function MyComponent({ ... }: Props) {
  return ( ... );
}
```

- One main export per file, named export matching the filename.
- Colocate types in the same file unless shared across modules.

## Shared state

| Context | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `AuthContext` | logged-in user, logout |
| `AuthSidebarContext` | login/register sidebar |
| `CartContext` | cart items and sidebar |

Do not prop-drill auth/cart when a context already exists.

## Scope and quality

- Match existing patterns in the same folder before inventing new abstractions.
- Prefer extending existing components over duplicating markup.
- Only add `"use client"` boundaries as small as necessary for interactivity.
- Do not create markdown/docs files unless explicitly requested.
